#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:1
msgid ""
"normalize-package-data [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/npm"
"/normalize-package-data.png?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/npm"
"/normalize-package-data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:3
msgid ""
"normalize-package-data exports a function that normalizes package "
"metadata. This data is typically found in a package.json file, but in "
"principle could come from any source - for example the npm registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:5
msgid ""
"normalize-package-data is used by [read-package-"
"json](https://npmjs.org/package/read-package-json) to normalize the data "
"it reads from a package.json file. In turn, read-package-json is used by "
"[npm](https://npmjs.org/package/npm) and various npm-related tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:7
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:13
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:15
msgid ""
"Basic usage is really simple. You call the function that normalize-"
"package-data exports. Let's call it `normalizeData`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:24
msgid "Strict mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:26
msgid "You may activate strict validation by passing true as the second argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:35
msgid ""
"If strict mode is activated, only Semver 2.0 version strings are "
"accepted. Otherwise, Semver 1.0 strings are accepted as well. Packages "
"must have a name, and the name field must not have contain leading or "
"trailing whitespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:37
msgid "Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:39
msgid ""
"Optionally, you may pass a \"warning\" function. It gets called whenever "
"the `normalizeData` function encounters something that doesn't look "
"right. It indicates less than perfect input data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:49
msgid ""
"You may combine strict validation with warnings by passing `true` as the "
"second argument, and `warnFn` as third."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:51
msgid "When `private` field is set to `true`, warnings will be suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:53
msgid "Potential exceptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:55
msgid ""
"If the supplied data has an invalid name or version vield, "
"`normalizeData` will throw an error. Depending on where you call "
"`normalizeData`, you may want to catch these errors so can pass them to a"
" callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:57
msgid "What normalization (currently) entails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:59
msgid "The value of `name` field gets trimmed (unless in strict mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:60
msgid ""
"The value of the `version` field gets cleaned by `semver.clean`. See "
"[documentation for the semver module](https://github.com/isaacs/node-"
"semver)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:61
msgid ""
"If `name` and/or `version` fields are missing, they are set to empty "
"strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:62
msgid "If `files` field is not an array, it will be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:63
msgid ""
"If `bin` field is a string, then `bin` field will become an object with "
"`name` set to the value of the `name` field, and `bin` set to the "
"original string value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:64
msgid ""
"If `man` field is a string, it will become an array with the original "
"string as its sole member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:65
msgid ""
"If `keywords` field is string, it is considered to be a list of keywords "
"separated by one or more white-space characters. It gets converted to an "
"array by splitting on `\\s+`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:66
msgid ""
"All people fields (`author`, `maintainers`, `contributors`) get converted"
" into objects with name, email and url properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:67
msgid ""
"If `bundledDependencies` field (a typo) exists and `bundleDependencies` "
"field does not, `bundledDependencies` will get renamed to "
"`bundleDependencies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:68
msgid ""
"If the value of any of the dependencies fields  (`dependencies`, "
"`devDependencies`, `optionalDependencies`) is a string, it gets converted"
" into an object with familiar `name=>value` pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:69
msgid ""
"The values in `optionalDependencies` get added to `dependencies`. The "
"`optionalDependencies` array is left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:70
msgid ""
"As of v2: Dependencies that point at known hosted git providers "
"(currently: github, bitbucket, gitlab) will have their URLs "
"canonicalized, but protocols will be preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:71
msgid ""
"As of v2: Dependencies that use shortcuts for hosted git providers "
"(`org/proj`, `github:org/proj`, `bitbucket:org/proj`, `gitlab:org/proj`, "
"`gist:docid`) will have the shortcut left in place. (In the case of "
"github, the `org/proj` form will be expanded to `github:org/proj`.) THIS "
"MARKS A BREAKING CHANGE FROM V1, where the shorcut was previously "
"expanded to a URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:72
msgid ""
"If `description` field does not exist, but `readme` field does, then "
"(more or less) the first paragraph of text that's found in the readme is "
"taken as value for `description`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:73
msgid ""
"If `repository` field is a string, it will become an object with `url` "
"set to the original string value, and `type` set to `\"git\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:74
msgid ""
"If `repository.url` is not a valid url, but in the style of \"[owner-name"
"]/[repo-name]\", `repository.url` will be set to git+https://github.com"
"/[owner-name]/[repo-name].git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:75
msgid ""
"If `bugs` field is a string, the value of `bugs` field is changed into an"
" object with `url` set to the original string value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:76
msgid ""
"If `bugs` field does not exist, but `repository` field points to a "
"repository hosted on GitHub, the value of the `bugs` field gets set to an"
" url in the form of https://github.com/[owner-name]/[repo-name]/issues . "
"If the repository field points to a GitHub Gist repo url, the associated "
"http url is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:77
msgid ""
"If `bugs` field is an object, the resulting value only has email and url "
"properties. If email and url properties are not strings, they are "
"ignored. If no valid values for either email or url is found, bugs field "
"will be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:78
msgid "If `homepage` field is not a string, it will be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:79
msgid ""
"If the url in the `homepage` field does not specify a protocol, then http"
" is assumed. For example, `myproject.org` will be changed to "
"`http://myproject.org`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:80
msgid ""
"If `homepage` field does not exist, but `repository` field points to a "
"repository hosted on GitHub, the value of the `homepage` field gets set "
"to an url in the form of https://github.com/[owner-name]/[repo-"
"name]#readme . If the repository field points to a GitHub Gist repo url, "
"the associated http url is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:82
msgid "Rules for name field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:84
msgid ""
"If `name` field is given, the value of the name field must be a string. "
"The string may not:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:86
msgid "start with a period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:87
msgid "contain the following characters: `/@\\s+%`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:88
msgid "contain any characters that would need to be encoded for use in urls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:89
msgid "resemble the word `node_modules` or `favicon.ico` (case doesn't matter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:91
msgid "Rules for version field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:93
msgid ""
"If `version` field is given, the value of the version field must be a "
"valid *semver* string, as determined by the `semver.valid` method. See "
"[documentation for the semver module](https://github.com/isaacs/node-"
"semver)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:95
msgid "Rules for license field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/normalize-package-data_README.md:97
msgid ""
"The `license` field should be a valid *SPDX license expression* or one of"
" the special values allowed by [validate-npm-package-"
"license](https://npmjs.com/package/validate-npm-package-license). See "
"[documentation for the license field in "
"package.json](https://docs.npmjs.com/files/package.json#license)."
msgstr ""

